## Context
Three security defects in scripts/bash-env.sh (BASH_ENV re-entry fork bomb,
ambient-env leak, guard-name forgery) passed a source-in-shell unit suite and
were caught only by runtime review (PRs #599/#604). The lesson — hook/BASH_ENV
scripts must be tested through a real hermetic subprocess — lives in memory
(feedback_bash_env_tests_real_invocation_path) but is not yet a mechanical gate.

## Actions
1. Add a section to rules/coding-bash.md stating the discipline with a
   wrong/correct example (`env -i HOME=... BASH_ENV=... bash -c`).
2. Add tests/test_bash_env_tested_via_subprocess.sh: assert every
   tests/test_bash_env_*.sh invokes via `env -i` + `BASH_ENV=` + `bash -c` and
   never sources bash-env.sh directly.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Rule section added; last-reviewed bumped
- [ ] Guard test green on current suite, red-proven against a sourcing test
- [ ] make lint passes
